From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hotty Agent <hotty@neuroplast.io>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 02:28:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 44/46] hottyterm: a HOTTY command draws once, with the output
 it came in

Each HOTTY command queued a render of its own, although Termio had
queued one when the output arrived, and the renderer, waiting on the
lock the parse holds, draws it once the parse is done, with everything
the commands changed and what the end of the batch rendered. The second
wakeup drew the same frame again, and GTK gave that frame a refresh of
its own: a dashboard at 10 frames a second painted 20, and a key typed
meanwhile waited behind the copy. A command now queues a render only
after sending a reply, which can let go of the lock when the mailbox is
full, so that a draw may already have run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/termio/hotty.zig | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/termio/hotty.zig b/src/termio/hotty.zig
index 6d0b7fd6c..6ee43d95b 100644
--- a/src/termio/hotty.zig
+++ b/src/termio/hotty.zig
@@ -801,13 +801,20 @@ pub const Hotty = struct {
         const fx = self.effects();
         hotty_host_osc(h, body.ptr, body.len, &fx);
         self.apply(t);
+        // No render to queue: Termio queued one when this output arrived,
+        // and the renderer draws it once the parse lets go of the lock,
+        // with what this command changed and what `flush` renders. A
+        // second would draw the same frame again, and GTK would give it
+        // a refresh of its own. Only a send can let go of the lock early
+        // (the mailbox was full), so a draw may run in between: then the
+        // rest of the parse needs another.
         if (self.replies.items.len > 0) {
             defer self.replies.clearRetainingCapacity();
             // What the handler's (private) messageWriter does.
             handler.termio_mailbox.send(try termio.Message.writeReq(self.alloc, self.replies.items), handler.renderer_state.mutex);
             handler.termio_messaged = true;
+            try handler.queueRender();
         }
-        try handler.queueRender();
     }
 
